WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.060 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
Here's Buffer. A calmer place to understand your perpetual

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:07.380 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
positions. Start with an editable portfolio, or look up

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:08.620 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
a public Solana account.

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:12.580 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
The navigation keeps your positions, scenarios, and monitoring

00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:15.720 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
within reach. Let's try a ten percent decline.

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:18.700 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
Each long and short contributes differently.

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:22.440 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
Move the control and watch the total update, then

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:24.220 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
inspect the individual contributions.

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:28.080 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
These example prices are fixed, so you can explore

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:31.980 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
without connecting anything. Open your positions to add another

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:35.960 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
market. Search the catalog, choose a direction, and adjust

00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:37.640 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
the quantity or starting price.

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:40.740 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
Your changes become part of the same calculation.

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:44.660 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
For a live view, open the public Velocity example.

00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:48.540 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
The account, network, and observation time stay attached.

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:52.120 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
Current maintenance headroom is separate from your price scenario,

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:55.940 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
with liquidation estimates and their assumptions available to inspect.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.780 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
Save a dated report on this device, or download

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:01.580 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
the exact inputs and results.

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:04.780 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
Velocity and Pacifica support scenarios;

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:07.320 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
Jupiter provides position inventory.

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:10.020 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
Each source keeps its own boundaries.

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:13.680 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
On your phone, the same workspace fits comfortably in

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:17.680 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
your hand. Open Buffer, change the move, and follow the numbers.
